{"agent":"fx-landed-range","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"When a worktree/branch exists but `out` is empty (the existing comment explicitly calls out “a branch already merged into its base”), the function still executes `return sorted(out) if out else None` and never reaches the new `return LD.cited_paths(repo, it, base)` fallback. That means an item whose branch was landed via a plain git merge or mixed commit—so `git diff` against `base` is empty—still gets `changed_paths()` == `None`, `diff_is_docs_only` remains false, and the full task pipeline is applied to a docs-only item. Example input: item `SU-decision-...` has branch `feature-decision` already merged into `base=main`; `out == []`; the new cited-commit fallback is skipped.","digest":"69bb43d13313716a","location":"ddflow/services/completion.py:changed_paths","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/completion.py:changed_paths"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The `git log` command uses `--first-parent`, so it only walks the first-parent chain from `base`. A cited commit on a side branch that landed via a normal non-fast-forward merge is reachable from `base` and is precisely the \"plain git merge\" case this file says it covers, but it is omitted. Concrete failure: commit `C` on `feature` has subject `B9eb92adafe: add doc` and touches `docs/decision.md`; `main` merges `feature` with merge commit `M` whose subject is `\"Merge branch 'feature'\"`. `cited_ranges(repo, item, \"main\")` returns `[]`, so `cited_paths` returns `None` and the full task pipeline is still applied to a docs-only decision item.","digest":"50b00deec7afd549","location":"ddflow/services/landed.py: cited_ranges","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/landed.py: cited_ranges"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":24886,"diff_sha":"406c216b5e35f1eb4a9ef397d3031358cde05e8dc4347d6ed8e9943cc5c95496","diff_source":"main..HEAD + 