{"agent":"fx-landed-range","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"A cited commit that cannot be diffed is silently omitted instead of forcing `cited_paths` to return `None`. For a cited root commit, `%P` is empty, so `if not first or not _cites(...): continue` discards it even though its subject cites the item. If a later cited commit verifiably changes only docs, `cited_paths` still returns that docs path rather than `None`. Concrete input: base has a root commit `B9: initial work` touching `src/code.py` and `docs/decision.md`, and a later commit `B9: add decision` touching only `docs/decision.md`; the root commit is dropped, `cited_paths` returns `docs/decision.md`, and `diff_is_docs_only` skips the full task pipeline despite a cited commit that touched code.","digest":"03c10fa2c5995bfc","location":"ddflow/services/landed.py:cited_ranges","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/landed.py:cited_ranges"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`cited_ranges` matches commits across all of `base` by the human-chosen `item.id` alone. [D-B191-item-ids-accepted] says the same id can be reused via `--readd` after removal, but the function has no notion of the current item's lifetime or definition. A removed item's old nil-cited docs commit remains in `base`; after `B9` is readded with overlapping declared globs and no branch, that old commit is returned as the new item's landing, so `cited_paths`/`diff_is_docs_only` can classify the unlanded new item as docs-only.","digest":"32454e379a4380f2","location":"ddflow/services/landed.py:cited_ranges","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/landed.py:cited_ranges"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"The early full-scope return still runs the whole suite for the exact item this change is meant to fix. For a docs-only decision item whose effective pipeline omits the CI gate, `_ci_not_passed_here` sees `\"ci\" not in _pipeline(cfg, it, tree)` and returns the \"no ci gate...\" reason; line 108 then returns `Scope(\"full\", why, needs_ci=False)`. A `Scope(\"full\")` still makes the test runner execute the full suite, so required unit_tests still apply to a docs-only item (B9eb92adafe), even though the pipeline was reduced. The docs-only effective pipeline should suppress this fallback; as written it only changes the `needs_ci` flag.","digest":"861d41773ff5ecdd","location":"ddflow/services/testscope.py:108","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/testscope.py:108"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The new regression tests only create default-kind `task` items via `_unmerged_task` (`run_cli(repo, \"task\", \"add\", \"T1\", ...)` with no `--kind`). The intent explicitly names `research`-kind items (B75d2b12ff1) as still excluded from docs-only and says to include kind research. No test constructs a `kind=\"research\"` item with a docs-only cited commit, and the pre-existing assertion at line 147 still expects `not diff_is_docs_only(it, cfg, [\"docs/x.md\"])`. Thus a version that leaves `diff_is_docs_only` returning False for `kind != \"task\"` — the reported bug — still passes all newly added tests, or, if the fix does change `diff_is_docs_only` for research, that unchanged assertion fails and breaks the suite.","digest":"a6a9d5a88f6ccea0","location":"tests/test_docs_only_task_pipeline.py:147","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_docs_only_task_pipeline.py:147"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":27187,"diff_sha":"5258c5cc525ad9f61b7ea07f62e35674d4074e26eebd2e9020dc42eb8d04799d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":823.7,"excluded_bytes":2775,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr"],"family":"deepseek","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"64c73879339249a5","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B9eb92adafe.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261021T180250Z-75290ffa.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewed_head":"063efee7fa9eb8a10763d37bc8f7352965fa8f59","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/batch.py":"100644 38543f36d999ab023b3d241f0ba62d2bf72017df","ddflow/api/items.py":"100644 aba31e93ba760640dc43ab4c8f3e89a3660f03eb","ddflow/api/mergequeue_run.py":"100644 f9e39d48311e62471aba267a03162441b254419e","ddflow/core/handlers/items.py":"100644 6ed62cbb7ed8f3e67fda5cdc1cb70d16cae2ea9d","ddflow/services/completion.py":"100644 bfac1195605a52c53bb1962a1c2f2a7a7cbc7570","ddflow/services/landed.py":"100644 111b3ff54d20e84a9e0757428d668ecff72d67eb","ddflow/services/pipeline_diff.py":"100644 23836d5b4ff56791f29c8c8555f1cd41a7403871","ddflow/services/report.py":"100644 de89e58f95e3e7ea1d390cf871dd9bb7128581a1","ddflow/services/report_gates.py":"100644 6819030f3c3aba804d32a1e01dbfa84035a8f763","ddflow/services/testscope.py":"100644 a507aed228f8f106fc13c2753d9a958f1c2471f5","ddflow/services/verify.py":"100644 b3f64da244d3e3992053c2f04cb1946c12823b54","ddflow/surfaces/declared/queue.py":"100644 8ff30621a1044feba9b2afd349172a64eaff9758","ddflow/views/markdown.py":"100644 63c890c707c312cd9850668bf12935acca5fdf29","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr":"100644 a800e551df09a3aa67f550c5eaa96aaba7ef9a00","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr":"100644 9f230928d97ad3d7d098ecc9ef7d820a75a56dae","tests/test_docs_only_task_pipeline.py":"100644 023221eb2dd176fd55fa39d46ec76af506d56b29"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","round":2,"rounds":2,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/landed.py:cited_ranges","ddflow/services/landed.py:cited_ranges","ddflow/services/testscope.py:108","tests/test_docs_only_task_pipeline.py:147"],"tree_sha":"063efee7fa9e+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"4 finding(s)"},"id":"ebfc33433a79f37b49019aa2b","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":89426,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B9eb92adafe","ts":"2026-10-21T18:16:34.660830Z"}
{"agent":"fx-landed-range","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_landed_fields` validates `--landed` against `it.base` (or the default base) before `plan_edit` applies the same update's `edit.base`. If a single update changes `base` and sets `landed`, the landed commit is checked against the outgoing base. Concretely: item has `base=main` and no landed range; commit `c` is on `main` but not on `release/1`; `update` with `base=release/1` and `landed=c` passes `LD.check` against `main`, then records `base=release/1` and `landed_after=c`, leaving the item with a landed commit that is not on its base. The check should use `edit.base` when provided, since that is the post-update base being recorded.","digest":"3ef4d667516232e5","location":"ddflow/api/items.py:_landed_fields","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/items.py:_landed_fields"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The change delegates the docs-only pipeline decision to the existing `docsonly.pipeline_by_diff`, but the manifest contains no modification to `ddflow/services/docsonly.py`, so the pre-existing `diff_is_docs_only` guard that rejects `item.kind != 'task'` remains. As a result, a research item (`RM-*`/`RV-*`) whose only changed path is a doc file still receives the full declared research pipeline. Example: an item `RM-decision-1` with only `docs/decision.md` in `changed_paths(repo, item)` calls `effective_pipeline(repo, cfg, item)`; `pipeline_by_diff` returns `(base, False)` because the item kind is not `task`, so `report.py` and other callers of this new choke point still apply the full research/testing pipeline, leaving the stated B75d2b12ff1 bug unresolved.","digest":"64a7f248b60a9200","location":"ddflow/services/pipeline_diff.py:20 effective_pipeline","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/pipeline_diff.py:20 effective_pipeline"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The stated fix for B9eb92adafe requires `diff_is_docs_only` to include kind `\"research\"`, but the existing assertion `assert not diff_is_docs_only(it, cfg, [\"docs/x.md\"])` for `Item(id=\"X\", kind=\"research\", title=\"t\", globs=[\"docs/x.md\"])` is left unchanged. Given the intended change, running this regression test will hit that assertion and fail; the test must be updated or removed, and no new test covers a cited docs-only `research` item.","digest":"19b053bc81e471f8","location":"tests/test_docs_only_task_pipeline.py:147","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_docs_only_task_pipeline.py:147"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"5/6 chunk(s) reviewed, 1 off-contract","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":27187,"diff_sha":"5258c5cc525ad9f61b7ea07f62e35674d4074e26eebd2e9020dc42eb8d04799d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1113.9,"excluded_bytes":2775,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr"],"family":"deepseek","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"d485e5347fb56841","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B9eb92adafe.critic.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261021T180250Z-003216ad.jsonl","reason":"1 of 6 chunk(s) not reviewed:\n  chunk 3/6 (ddflow/services/landed.py): came back OFF CONTRACT: 986 chars with no STATUS: block. Not counted as reviewed.","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,4,5,6],"reviewed_head":"063efee7fa9eb8a10763d37bc8f7352965fa8f59","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/batch.py":"100644 38543f36d999ab023b3d241f0ba62d2bf72017df","ddflow/api/items.py":"100644 aba31e93ba760640dc43ab4c8f3e89a3660f03eb","ddflow/api/mergequeue_run.py":"100644 f9e39d48311e62471aba267a03162441b254419e","ddflow/core/handlers/items.py":"100644 6ed62cbb7ed8f3e67fda5cdc1cb70d16cae2ea9d","ddflow/services/completion.py":"100644 bfac1195605a52c53bb1962a1c2f2a7a7cbc7570","ddflow/services/landed.py":"1